ested or reported in the paper."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Body_mass_index", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited Wikipedia article describes what BMI is, its categories, uses, limitations and health associations, but it does not provide empirical evidence or discussion linking higher group-level BMI to greater physical space requirements, interpersonal spacing, or an expanded spatial scale of group activities. No studies or data about seating/movement space or changes in interaction scale are cited in the provided content. Therefore the explanation’s causal claim is not supported by the source."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Higher group-level BMI directly causes an increase in the spatial scale at which individuals interact, because groups with higher average BMI require more physical space for movement and seating. This increased physical spacing at the group level leads to a measurable expansion in the spatial scale of group activities.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Higher group-level BMI directly causes an increase in the spatial scale at which individuals interact, because groups with higher average BMI require more physical space for movement and seating. This increased physical spacing at the group level leads to a measurable expansion in the spatial scale of group activities.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

