 not fully prove the asserted no-direct-causation claim."}], "aggregate_score": 0.25, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) does not directly cause Total Daily Energy Intake (TDEI). While energy expenditure may influence hunger or appetite through physiological mechanisms, the direct causal relationship is mediated by behavioral and biological factors such as hunger signals and food availability. Therefore, there is no direct causal link from TDEE to TDEI in the absence of these mediating variables.', 'aggregate_score': 0.25, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.3719899486412956, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8207645761982292, 'min_prob': 0.010464444411847993, 'token_prob_slope': -0.002174874855977052, 'prob_variance': 0.07066729188928178, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9661534408049472, 'avg_nll': 0.31626220321366216}

