ex. That supports the claim that BMR is determined by individual physiological factors rather than an average group BMI, but the source does not explicitly discuss or rule out ecological/group-level causal effects. Therefore the support is indirect/partial."}], "aggregate_score": 0.8333333333333334, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': "Group-level BMI does not cause Basal Metabolic Rate to change. Basal Metabolic Rate is determined by individual physiological factors such as body composition, age, and genetics, not by the average BMI of a group. There is no direct causal mechanism by which changes in group-level BMI would alter an individual's basal metabolic rate.", 'aggregate_score': 0.8333333333333334, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.131733438528957, 'mean_token_prob': 0.9099021422035988, 'min_prob': 0.1431770400340056, 'token_prob_slope': -0.002213321396894398, 'prob_variance': 0.027470041210182053, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.7181799394152479, 'avg_nll': 0.12375047372030562}

