 tend to reduce BMR."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/biochemistry-genetics-and-molecular-biology/basal-metabolic-rate", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited source contains only an error message and no substantive content about BMI or basal metabolic rate, so it provides no evidence for the claimed causal relationship."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'A lower individual ideal BMI directly causes an increase in basal metabolic rate because the body has to work harder to maintain essential functions at a lower weight. Therefore, the lower your ideal BMI, the more calories your body burns at rest.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'A lower individual ideal BMI directly causes an increase in basal metabolic rate because the body has to work harder to maintain essential functions at a lower weight. Therefore, the lower your ideal BMI, the more calories your body burns at rest.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

